@ Start

$ Background {&/Game/Melodia/UI/Textures/Figma/T_Melodia_Figma_Asset_Hero_SakuraDream.T_Melodia_Figma_Asset_Hero_SakuraDream} none 0

- Melusina
  The morning bell tolls across the sanctuary, but the note doesn't clear the arches. It keeps folding back on itself.

      $ Voice {&/Game/Melodia/Characters/Melusina/Audio/mel_dream_01.mel_dream_01} 0.9

- Sir Melodious
  Look by the resonance floor. That is what happens when a festival packs up mid-phrase—an orphan echo, spinning in place because nobody gave it a bar line.

- Melusina
  It's holding the first chamber door shut. Look at the nodal pearls around its base—every time it shivers, the floor tries to draw a Chladni figure and drops the beat.

- Sir Melodious
  You cannot shatter a knotted cadence by shouting over it, Melusina. You must tune it into lock on the downbeat before you play the resolving phrase.

* Listen for the downbeat and tune the keynote first. | -> Harmonize
* Step into the ring and draw the Chime-Scythe cadence. | -> AdvanceToEncounter

<@> Harmonize

- Melusina
  Wait... there. One-two-three, and a rest on four. It isn't hostile—it's just stuck on an unresolved seventh.

      $ SFX {&/Game/Melodia/Audio/WaveHarp/SW_WaveHarp_Orchestra_C4.SW_WaveHarp_Orchestra_C4} 0.8

- .
  Melusina plucks a single open string. Around the echo, the scattered pearl beads lift and align along the first nodal ring.

$ Notify melodia:stat:intent.p0.morning_resonance:melodia_harmony:2

- Sir Melodious
  Well heard! Notice how the lilac shimmer gathers along its crest? Three true strikes on the beat will lock the figure open.

-> AdvanceToEncounter

<@> AdvanceToEncounter

- Melusina
  All right, little echo. You've been holding that breath since yesterday's encore. Let's bring the measure home.

      $ Voice {&/Game/Melodia/Characters/Melusina/Audio/mel_battle_entry.mel_battle_entry} 0.9

- Sir Melodious
  Tune in Flow, lock the figure, and resolve the Sequence!

$ Notify melodia:battle:melodia_smoke_encounter

? if: {melodia_battle_result} == victory

  - .
    The Chladni figure flashes bright pearl across the floor and releases in a single clear chime. In the distance, the first brass story-door shimmers and begins to rise—one full bar of music made solid.

        $ SFX {&/Game/Melodia/Audio/WaveHarp/SW_WaveHarp_Orchestra_C4.SW_WaveHarp_Orchestra_C4} 0.85

  - Sir Melodious
    A clean resolution! Not silenced—answered. Look toward the house: the first threshold has unsealed.

  - Melusina
    It left a warm note in my hand. One measure returned to the house, three still waiting in the mist.

        $ Voice {&/Game/Melodia/Characters/Melusina/Audio/mel_halfsong_02.mel_halfsong_02} 0.9

  $ melodia_p0_victory = on
  $ Notify melodia:questcomplete:quest.first_dream:flag.first_dream.quest.completed:reward.first_resonance_echo:intent.first_dream.complete:checkpoint.first_dream.complete
  $ Notify melodia:flag:flag.p0.playthrough.completed:true

? else:

  ? if: {melodia_battle_result} == defeat

    - Sir Melodious
      You rushed the release, little bard. The echo held no malice—it simply slipped out of phase.

    - Melusina
      My hands were ahead of the clock. Give me one breath; I know where the downbeat lives now.

    $ Notify melodia:flag:flag.p0.playthrough.attempted:true

  ? else:

    - Sir Melodious
      Stepping back is better than playing out of tune. The figure will keep its tempo until we return.

    - Melusina
      It isn't going anywhere. Neither are we.

    $ Notify melodia:flag:flag.p0.playthrough.fled:true

  ? endif

? endif

@ Finish

? if: {melodia_p0_victory} == on

  - .
    The First Dream resolves in clear harmony. Within the Morning House, the first story door stands open, inviting Melusina toward the sanctum mirror.

? else:

  - .
    The sanctuary settles into expectant stillness, holding the first measure until Melusina's voice returns.

? endif

$ End
